<h1>Castings</h1>

<p>Our foundries in Sheffield and Poznan produce sand and investment castings in grey iron, ductile iron, carbon and low-alloy steel, and aluminium alloys. Typical part weights range from half a kilogram for small investment-cast fittings up to around four hundred and fifty kilograms for single-piece sand castings.</p>

<p>Pattern equipment is designed and built by our own tool room, which means changes to a casting design can usually be turned around without involving an outside supplier. Every casting is traced by heat number back to the original melt, and dimensional records are kept against the original drawing for the life of the contract.</p>

<table class="table">
    <thead>
        <tr><th>Process</th><th>Typical alloys</th><th>Weight range</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>No-bake sand casting</td><td>Grey iron, ductile iron, carbon steel</td><td>2 kg &ndash; 450 kg</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Shell moulding</td><td>Ductile iron, low-alloy steel</td><td>0.5 kg &ndash; 40 kg</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Investment casting</td><td>Stainless steel, aluminium alloys</td><td>0.1 kg &ndash; 12 kg</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<p>Most castings leave the foundry for further work in our own machining and finishing lines; see <a href="/products/machining">machining</a> for details. Pattern and core box development is covered under <a href="/products/tooling">tooling</a>.</p>
